<title>UK: BGB Finance sets 10 bln yen dual-currency bond. [CORRECTED 19:02 GMT]</title>
<headline>BGB Finance sets 10 bln yen dual-currency bond. [CORRECTED 19:02 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Credit Suisse First Boston.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE (IRELAND) PLC</p>
<p> AMT    10 BLN YEN    COUPON    **3.36	MATURITY  **12.MAR.07</p>
<p> TYPE   DUAL-CURRENCY ISS PRICE  PAR	 PAY DATE    12.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  NONE	LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> MOODY/S&amp;P  =	   DENOMS (M) 100	 SALE LIMITS ***</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> GUARANTOR BGB, BERLINER BANK AND LANDESBANK BERLIN GIROZENTRALE</p>
<p>	     WITH A RATING OF AA1 BY MOODY'S</p>
<p>	    **COUPON IN U.S. DOLLARS, REDEMPTION IN YEN</p>
<p>	   ***US/UK/DE/JP/IE</p>
<p>(corrects to show that the coupon is in U.S. Dollars and the redemption is in Yen, instead of the other way around)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
